+   read so far, open or closed, with the bytes read from it and whether it
+   reached the end (1 or 0), then says
+                        file <pid> <bytes> <eof> <path>
+                        snapshot <id> <n> <pos> <pid> <child-pid>
+   With <every> and <max>, the child takes snapshots only after pages that
+   are multiples of <every>, and at most <max> of them (0: none).
+   Paused processes form a chain (engine, snapshots, the running child):
+   one reads commands only while it has no child.  To cancel a run, the
+   driver kills its child; to run from a snapshot (the bytes it read from
+   each file unchanged, and no more of a file it read to the end), it kills
+   the snapshots after it and waits for "resumed".  A run reads every input
